Barrage prepares one combat working to cast automatically beside ordinary
attacks. Mana Shard, Missile, Fireball, Icestorm, and Bolt are eligible.

Without a FOCUS weapon, the page must be Practiced and each automatic cast
spends SP. With FOCUS, even a Copied page can be prepared and fires for zero SP.
AURA completes battlemage resonance and improves cadence and power. Mastery
and Falx can quicken the rhythm, but two combat rounds is the ordinary floor.

At Arcane 16, a real wielded FOCUS opens a more severe exchange. The prepared
page fires every combat round and produces multiple complete barrages. Their
count is based on the FOCUS weapon's WC and item level, not the Mage's ordinary
number of swings:

  barrages = 1 + floor((10 * WC + item level) / 100), from 2 to 6

The same weave removes weapon swings according to player level: one below 50,
two at 50, three at 100, four at 150, five at 200, and six at 250 or above.
Investiture's borrowed FOCUS cannot enable this exchange. Releasing the
prepared barrage removes the penalty.

Concentration pauses cadence without erasing the page. Silence or paralysis
collapses it. Automatic casts still teach mastery and can earn rate-limited
field GXP.

Use "barrage <working>", "barrage off", and "battlemage".
